<%# A heading and a paragraph, using the same section head as every other block.

  THIS TYPE IS NOT THE WHOLE ABOUT PAGE ANY MORE. It used to be four of these in a row, which is what the
  design system's rule 2 forbids -- the About page now runs prose -> note -> prose -> cards, so this partial
  sets one subject at a time rather than carrying a page's entire rhythm on its own
  (Marketing::ContentBlueprint#about_page says why each of the two recasts is the better type).
%>
<section class="<%= tone %>">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
    <%= render 'marketing/shared/section_head', heading: section['heading'], lede: nil %>
    <% if section['body'].present? %>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-[1.8] text-lyn-ink-soft"><%= section['body'] %></p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>
